From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pessi-v <pessimo@posteo.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:38:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] (lilac) drm: treat rotation 0 as DRM_MODE_ROTATE_0

The msm8998 display stack from Android 9 sets the plane rotation
property to 0 to mean "no rotation". 4.14 requires exactly one rotation
bit and fails the whole atomic commit with EINVAL, so nothing was ever
shown. Read "no rotation bits" as ROTATE_0; values with several rotation
bits are still refused.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c |   14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c
index a87ead3c5c20938a341d438e03ab47e0b2d34f35..5e0cb0f9441d7432e423e4cb0e93fc3b8529d389 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c
@@ -764,6 +764,20 @@ static int drm_atomic_plane_set_property(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	} else if (property == config->prop_src_h) {
 		state->src_h = val;
 	} else if (property == plane->rotation_property) {
+		/*
+		 * lilac: msm8998's Android 9 SDM sends rotation=0 to
+		 * mean "no rotation". The ABI spells that DRM_MODE_ROTATE_0
+		 * (== 1) and wants exactly one rotate bit, so is_power_of_2(0)
+		 * refuses it and the whole atomic commit fails EINVAL -- which
+		 * is why the display was never programmed at all.
+		 *
+		 * 4.4, which these blobs were built against, had no check here
+		 * and simply stored the value, so the distinction was never
+		 * forced on them. Read "no bits" as ROTATE_0, which is what the
+		 * caller means; ambiguous multi-bit values are still refused.
+		 */
+		if (!(val & DRM_MODE_ROTATE_MASK))
+			val |= DRM_MODE_ROTATE_0;
 		if (!is_power_of_2(val & DRM_MODE_ROTATE_MASK))
 			return -EINVAL;
 		state->rotation = val;
